(5286204, 767959, 59415, '<td valign="top">Oh ya that is one of those things that...um you know that keeps the...wait let me get on wikipedia... oh ya, these circular rings is a small terrestrial globe J, fixed on an axis K, which extends from the north and south poles of the globe at n and s, to those of the celestial sphere at N and S. On this axis is fixed the flat celestial meridian L L, which may be set directly over the meridian of any place on the globe, so as to keep over the same meridian upon it. This flat meridian is graduated the same way as the brass meridian of the common globe, and its use is much the same.  I knew that.</td>', 'Oh ya that is one of those things that...um you know that keeps the...wait let me get on wikipedia... oh ya, these circular rings is a small terrestrial globe J, fixed on an axis K, which extends from the north and south poles of the globe at n and s, to those of the celestial sphere at N and S. On this axis is fixed the flat celestial meridian L L, which may be set directly over the meridian of any place on the globe, so as to keep over the same meridian upon it. This flat meridian is graduated the same way as the brass meridian of the common globe, and its use is much the same.  I knew that.', '2009-03-03 19:03:25.000000', NULL, 1),
