(5293511, 763245, 82985, '<td valign="top">A wonderful image.  I am not anti-border in principle, but I find this border to be distracting.  It really draws the eye to the border with that dominating, bright color, and doesn''t really accent the small reddish elements in the image itself.  A pure black border, or no border, would serve this very nice image much better, in my opinion. 6</td>', 'A wonderful image.  I am not anti-border in principle, but I find this border to be distracting.  It really draws the eye to the border with that dominating, bright color, and doesn''t really accent the small reddish elements in the image itself.  A pure black border, or no border, would serve this very nice image much better, in my opinion. 6', '2009-03-06 22:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5293513, 768904, 88204, '<td valign="top">Great lighting. Interesting pose. It''s odd that her hair is falling sideways.</td>', 'Great lighting. Interesting pose. It''s odd that her hair is falling sideways.', '2009-03-06 22:21:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5293514, 768652, 88204, '<td valign="top">Fun shot! Great expression and eyes!</td>', 'Fun shot! Great expression and eyes!', '2009-03-06 22:22:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5293517, 768729, 88204, '<td valign="top">Interesting colors and lines.</td>', 'Interesting colors and lines.', '2009-03-06 22:24:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5293518, 769078, 88204, '<td valign="top">Very striking. Nice bokeh.</td>', 'Very striking. Nice bokeh.', '2009-03-06 22:24:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5293521, 765858, 88204, '<td valign="top">Great lighting. His face really pops. I''d like to know more about your lighting setup. I''m guessing you have a softbox or umbrella on both sides at about 45 degrees. Slight criticism: The background almost looks fake because the light on him is so sharp and considerably lighter. I think the strobes would be a little more natural if you brought up the ambient slightly. Then again, this has a very unique and punchy style exactly as is. My favorite so far. 10</td>', 'Great lighting. His face really pops. I''d like to know more about your lighting setup. I''m guessing you have a softbox or umbrella on both sides at about 45 degrees. Slight criticism: The background almost looks fake because the light on him is so sharp and considerably lighter. I think the strobes would be a little more natural if you brought up the ambient slightly. Then again, this has a very unique and punchy style exactly as is. My favorite so far. 10', '2009-03-06 22:29:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5293522, 768443, 88204, '<td valign="top">Gotta love those tongues! Great shot!</td>', 'Gotta love those tongues! Great shot!', '2009-03-06 22:29:45.000000', NULL, 1),
