(5295460, 768346, 102386, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ThingFish:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratz on the 9th place. Heck....so it was taken in South Africa as well. What a coincidence. When I placed my comment during voting I had no idea that it was in South Africa yet it reminded me of the times I spent fishing there in places such as this.<br/>I used to live in Witsand at the mouth of the Breede river and that strech of coastline looks just like this and I was often to be found there fishing at low tide just like the fisherman in your image.<br/>Now live in Holland but boy do I get homesick some times. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If you look closely, you''ll see Table Mountain in the background. Maybe it was that that caught your eye :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-03-08 11:14:41.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by ThingFish: Congratz on the 9th place. Heck....so it was taken in South Africa as well. What a coincidence. When I placed my comment during voting I had no idea that it was in South Africa yet it reminded me of the times I spent fishing there in places such as this.I used to live in Witsand at the mouth of the Breede river and that strech of coastline looks just like this and I was often to be found there fishing at low tide just like the fisherman in your image.Now live in Holland but boy do I get homesick some times.   If you look closely, you''ll see Table Mountain in the background. Maybe it was that that caught your eye :)', '2009-03-08 06:49:54.000000', '2009-03-08 11:14:41.000000', 0),
(5295465, 762717, 3746, '<td valign="top">Nice one mate... brilliant work as always.</td>', 'Nice one mate... brilliant work as always.', '2009-03-08 06:58:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5295468, 762717, 78455, '<td valign="top">Fantastic capture Keith! This is one of my lifelong dreams to get the opportunity to photograph these wonderfull creatures! You''ve done a fantastic job and I hope this is one of many pearls you''ve managed to bring back.</td>', 'Fantastic capture Keith! This is one of my lifelong dreams to get the opportunity to photograph these wonderfull creatures! You''ve done a fantastic job and I hope this is one of many pearls you''ve managed to bring back.', '2009-03-08 07:00:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5295473, 768395, 57886, '<td valign="top">Falleg mynd Bragi...  :o)</td>', 'Falleg mynd Bragi...  :o)', '2009-03-08 07:06:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5295482, 764971, 62357, '<td valign="top">Decent score!  I felt such a ''nana yesterday when I asked if you had something in the FS.  Doh!  Anyway, I still like it and am glad you got a decent score.</td>', 'Decent score!  I felt such a ''nana yesterday when I asked if you had something in the FS.  Doh!  Anyway, I still like it and am glad you got a decent score.', '2009-03-08 07:22:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5295483, 768687, 67258, '<td valign="top">Hi Ziggy, yo asked for some feedback on this photo.  Firstly, you have a very sweet looking grandchild, and those eyes and curls are gorgeous.  The focus on the eyes is sharp, and I am so glad you didn''t over-process them, as many on DPC have a tendency to.  I feel you could have afforded a very slightly deeper depth of field, so that the front curl was also in focus.  For me there were two things that struck me when I viewed this during voting - the slight appearance of ''dribble'' which I always find off-putting (strangely I never seemed to notice it in photos of my own children..)and the composition.  The cut-off head can sometimes work very well, but not, I feel, here.  Also, I do find the background rather distracting - a plain and even one would, I am sure, have resulted in a more pleasing image.  At the end of the day, there wasn''t enough about the photo to keep my attention.</td>', 'Hi Ziggy, yo asked for some feedback on this photo.  Firstly, you have a very sweet looking grandchild, and those eyes and curls are gorgeous.  The focus on the eyes is sharp, and I am so glad you didn''t over-process them, as many on DPC have a tendency to.  I feel you could have afforded a very slightly deeper depth of field, so that the front curl was also in focus.  For me there were two things that struck me when I viewed this during voting - the slight appearance of ''dribble'' which I always find off-putting (strangely I never seemed to notice it in photos of my own children..)and the composition.  The cut-off head can sometimes work very well, but not, I feel, here.  Also, I do find the background rather distracting - a plain and even one would, I am sure, have resulted in a more pleasing image.  At the end of the day, there wasn''t enough about the photo to keep my attention.', '2009-03-08 07:24:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5295490, 768991, 50641, '<td valign="top">oh look - this was you!  I really should have guessed from the title ;-)  like the dof here!</td>', 'oh look - this was you!  I really should have guessed from the title ;-)  like the dof here!', '2009-03-08 07:40:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5295492, 769100, 82707, '<td valign="top">WTG girl!  Congrats on the ribbon.....I''m sure Brit will love it!  I do!</td>', 'WTG girl!  Congrats on the ribbon.....I''m sure Brit will love it!  I do!', '2009-03-08 07:44:41.000000', NULL, 0),
