(5296894, 769083, 30982, '<td valign="top">If your title was supposed to clue me in on something, it didn''t.  I take it from comments below that it''s a movie of some kind?  And here I thought this was Wall "E" or some such.  This is what happens when you get socially and culturally ignorant viewers... :-)  At any rate, I liked the mess - I''ve seen a lot of messes like this behind trailers in Iraq and it reminded me of that, without the green plant.  My dislike (we''re all entitled!) is the selective desat - and that''s just a personal thing.  Is highlighting the plant some reference to the movie that I just didn''t get?</td>', 'If your title was supposed to clue me in on something, it didn''t.  I take it from comments below that it''s a movie of some kind?  And here I thought this was Wall "E" or some such.  This is what happens when you get socially and culturally ignorant viewers... :-)  At any rate, I liked the mess - I''ve seen a lot of messes like this behind trailers in Iraq and it reminded me of that, without the green plant.  My dislike (we''re all entitled!) is the selective desat - and that''s just a personal thing.  Is highlighting the plant some reference to the movie that I just didn''t get?', '2009-03-09 03:03:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296896, 768726, 30982, '<td valign="top">To me this begs the viewer to consider what may lay beyond.  That, and the cool light on the raindrops.  To me, this is a success - you got a Chromey PostLumie nod and a Ubique comment!</td>', 'To me this begs the viewer to consider what may lay beyond.  That, and the cool light on the raindrops.  To me, this is a success - you got a Chromey PostLumie nod and a Ubique comment!', '2009-03-09 03:05:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296897, 768547, 30982, '<td valign="top">Hee!  I need to get one of those Rinac filters... :-)</td>', 'Hee!  I need to get one of those Rinac filters... :-)', '2009-03-09 03:07:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296901, 768593, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''ll differ a bit on the "don''t use a centered horizon" part.  It CAN work but you have to have a reason to use it - symmetry, point of interest, etc.  For a simple landscape/waterscape shot, pick what you want to emphasize (water/ground or sky) and compose and crop accordingly.  There''s that lovely "rule of thirds" for composition that time has shown is generally pleasing to the eye.<br/> <br/>Also, your horizon may in fact not be tilted at all, but due to the natural curbature of the body of water.  The wake in the distance catching the light emphasizes that, and the overall EFFECT (but perhaps not reality) is a tilted horizon.  Again, it can work but only if there''s a distinct reason for it.  Here the "eye" wants it to be nice and level - less disconcerting that way.<br/> <br/>Finally, there are voters that have been at DPC for many years who tire of sunsets with no other point that a picture of a sunset.  Sounds harsh, but it is one possible reason for a lower than you expected score.</td>', 'I''ll differ a bit on the "don''t use a centered horizon" part.  It CAN work but you have to have a reason to use it - symmetry, point of interest, etc.  For a simple landscape/waterscape shot, pick what you want to emphasize (water/ground or sky) and compose and crop accordingly.  There''s that lovely "rule of thirds" for composition that time has shown is generally pleasing to the eye. Also, your horizon may in fact not be tilted at all, but due to the natural curbature of the body of water.  The wake in the distance catching the light emphasizes that, and the overall EFFECT (but perhaps not reality) is a tilted horizon.  Again, it can work but only if there''s a distinct reason for it.  Here the "eye" wants it to be nice and level - less disconcerting that way. Finally, there are voters that have been at DPC for many years who tire of sunsets with no other point that a picture of a sunset.  Sounds harsh, but it is one possible reason for a lower than you expected score.', '2009-03-09 03:14:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296905, 768789, 30982, '<td valign="top">This one made me laugh - then cry.  Why?  I realized that I am just as grumpy and mean-looking to someone who doesn''t know me and captures me staring blandly off into the distance.  Then it made me laugh again because why worry about stuff like that?  Entirely too busy for the DPC crowd and I will admit a bias to having annoying moving vehicles (as opposed to attractive moving vehicles) in a shot.  Here, were you able to hire a local policeman to help you out, you want that yellow taxi, but you want the rest of those idjits to get out of the way.  Then you have the nifty lady in blue, the younger more beautiful people across the way, the taxi, what appears to be phone booths or a bus stop, and the corporate overdose - and that would be just enough!</td>', 'This one made me laugh - then cry.  Why?  I realized that I am just as grumpy and mean-looking to someone who doesn''t know me and captures me staring blandly off into the distance.  Then it made me laugh again because why worry about stuff like that?  Entirely too busy for the DPC crowd and I will admit a bias to having annoying moving vehicles (as opposed to attractive moving vehicles) in a shot.  Here, were you able to hire a local policeman to help you out, you want that yellow taxi, but you want the rest of those idjits to get out of the way.  Then you have the nifty lady in blue, the younger more beautiful people across the way, the taxi, what appears to be phone booths or a bus stop, and the corporate overdose - and that would be just enough!', '2009-03-09 03:20:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296906, 768886, 30982, '<td valign="top">I really liked this - very natural, very warm.</td>', 'I really liked this - very natural, very warm.', '2009-03-09 03:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296909, 768794, 30982, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a great shot!  I came by because you claimed it was a sub-5.  Nice to see it moved out of that range and is worthy of a higher score.  Your commenters really appreciated it too!</td>', 'I thought this was a great shot!  I came by because you claimed it was a sub-5.  Nice to see it moved out of that range and is worthy of a higher score.  Your commenters really appreciated it too!', '2009-03-09 03:23:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296911, 766656, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh - just checked out Lynne''s and hers was a cat, too.  As with hers, this is a great kitty shot!  I always like kitty shots that show them being cats, doing what they do.  Wish mine would sit still long enough for that!  Gave you a 7, by the way.</td>', 'Heh - just checked out Lynne''s and hers was a cat, too.  As with hers, this is a great kitty shot!  I always like kitty shots that show them being cats, doing what they do.  Wish mine would sit still long enough for that!  Gave you a 7, by the way.', '2009-03-09 03:24:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296916, 769083, 52130, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> If your title was supposed to clue me in on something, it didn''t.  I take it from comments below that it''s a movie of some kind?  And here I thought this was Wall "E" or some such.  This is what happens when you get socially and culturally ignorant viewers... :-)  At any rate, I liked the mess - I''ve seen a lot of messes like this behind trailers in Iraq and it reminded me of that, without the green plant.  My dislike (we''re all entitled!) is the selective desat - and that''s just a personal thing.  Is highlighting the plant some reference to the movie that I just didn''t get? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Aha! So THAT was the problem! I had just assumed that WALL-E was way more popular than it apparently was. That was definitely my mistake then because I really thought that everyone had seen it by now (hope I don''t sound condecending to anyone because I''m being honest). Well then, if you haven''t seen WALL-E yet, go out and rent it because even though it''s an animated movie (that won an Oscar for best animated film and it''s by Pixar), I think it''s one of the best movies of all time :) Thanks for clarifying...my score makes so much more sense now.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-03-09 03:40:56.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: If your title was supposed to clue me in on something, it didn''t.  I take it from comments below that it''s a movie of some kind?  And here I thought this was Wall "E" or some such.  This is what happens when you get socially and culturally ignorant viewers... :-)  At any rate, I liked the mess - I''ve seen a lot of messes like this behind trailers in Iraq and it reminded me of that, without the green plant.  My dislike (we''re all entitled!) is the selective desat - and that''s just a personal thing.  Is highlighting the plant some reference to the movie that I just didn''t get?   Aha! So THAT was the problem! I had just assumed that WALL-E was way more popular than it apparently was. That was definitely my mistake then because I really thought that everyone had seen it by now (hope I don''t sound condecending to anyone because I''m being honest). Well then, if you haven''t seen WALL-E yet, go out and rent it because even though it''s an animated movie (that won an Oscar for best animated film and it''s by Pixar), I think it''s one of the best movies of all time :) Thanks for clarifying...my score makes so much more sense now.', '2009-03-09 03:40:19.000000', '2009-03-09 03:40:56.000000', 0),
(5296917, 769083, 52130, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RulerZigzag:</b></div><hr/><i> Oh wow, when I peeped this I was so happy to see more Wall-E fans out there, but the photo didn''t have the TV in it, or more collectibles, like the big ol shoe, and the lighter, and the roach, no pun intended...:( Way to rep Wall-E tho. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, this was just a snapshot I took in through an old abandoned window, and I wasn''t even really thinking of WALL-E when I took it. Yes, a T.V. or lighter would have been pretty cool, but I do have an old soda can and a battery with a recycle symbol on it :)</td>', 'Originally posted by RulerZigzag: Oh wow, when I peeped this I was so happy to see more Wall-E fans out there, but the photo didn''t have the TV in it, or more collectibles, like the big ol shoe, and the lighter, and the roach, no pun intended...:( Way to rep Wall-E tho.   Yeah, this was just a snapshot I took in through an old abandoned window, and I wasn''t even really thinking of WALL-E when I took it. Yes, a T.V. or lighter would have been pretty cool, but I do have an old soda can and a battery with a recycle symbol on it :)', '2009-03-09 03:43:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296921, 768593, 52130, '<td valign="top">I agree with the others, tilted horizon and it also looks a tad bit shakey...were you using a tripod or was the dock moving? The colors are very nice and it has good symmetry, but it leaves me wanting more, especially on the top and bottom.</td>', 'I agree with the others, tilted horizon and it also looks a tad bit shakey...were you using a tripod or was the dock moving? The colors are very nice and it has good symmetry, but it leaves me wanting more, especially on the top and bottom.', '2009-03-09 03:48:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296924, 768880, 30982, '<td valign="top">Jane, you do great birds!  I think this one suffered from a lack of sharpness more than anything else.  I also think a less centered presentation would have a stronger dynamic, but that said I kinda like the wide view.  Good look you captured, too - he certainly seems quite intent on something!</td>', 'Jane, you do great birds!  I think this one suffered from a lack of sharpness more than anything else.  I also think a less centered presentation would have a stronger dynamic, but that said I kinda like the wide view.  Good look you captured, too - he certainly seems quite intent on something!', '2009-03-09 03:50:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296927, 768739, 30982, '<td valign="top">My only suggestion would be to change out the red thread in the back - it has a tendency to pull the eye away from the point of interest.  Alternately, stick the fly on the red thread and move the other spool to the back.</td>', 'My only suggestion would be to change out the red thread in the back - it has a tendency to pull the eye away from the point of interest.  Alternately, stick the fly on the red thread and move the other spool to the back.', '2009-03-09 03:54:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5296935, 768963, 30982, '<td valign="top">Gentle and quite peaceful!  I think your score may have been hurt by a lack of clear subject (yeah, I know, this doesn''t really have or need one, but there you go) and a bit of a "halved" composition.  You''ve got a couple of elements I really like in the shot - the curved upper branch, the sun peeking through, the curve of the wall/bushes.  I''m just not sure I like how they''re all arranged with respect to each other if that makes sense, though I don''t know how else to arrange them - aren''t I helpful?</td>', 'Gentle and quite peaceful!  I think your score may have been hurt by a lack of clear subject (yeah, I know, this doesn''t really have or need one, but there you go) and a bit of a "halved" composition.  You''ve got a couple of elements I really like in the shot - the curved upper branch, the sun peeking through, the curve of the wall/bushes.  I''m just not sure I like how they''re all arranged with respect to each other if that makes sense, though I don''t know how else to arrange them - aren''t I helpful?', '2009-03-09 04:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
