(5297604, 769100, 80096, '<td valign="top">Amazing image, Judi, simply amazing! Congatulations on your 2nd place ribbon!</td>', 'Amazing image, Judi, simply amazing! Congatulations on your 2nd place ribbon!', '2009-03-09 12:22:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297611, 762717, 80096, '<td valign="top">This is a classic, a gem! You''re so lucky to have material like this to capture. A well deserved first place win!</td>', 'This is a classic, a gem! You''re so lucky to have material like this to capture. A well deserved first place win!', '2009-03-09 12:26:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297617, 769100, 68546, '<td valign="top">I can''t really add anymore then the others, this is stunning. Such great editing as well, really adds to the image and yet isn''t obviously edited. Great work</td>', 'I can''t really add anymore then the others, this is stunning. Such great editing as well, really adds to the image and yet isn''t obviously edited. Great work', '2009-03-09 12:30:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297624, 769141, 29011, '<td valign="top">Thanks so much, everyone. Really appreciate your kind comments. Very glad you like the shot. I honestly didn''t think it''d do this well in a FS. It''s a wonerful pleasant surprise. None of the details in the shot where blurred (except selective noise removal in the sky), I did crop the sides and had two b/w conversions to choose from, one which had a lighter sky color, but playing with the channels I do like how the darker sky came out in this one but the feather detail was better in the color version. Also, updated the exif.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-03-09 12:40:42.</i></td>', 'Thanks so much, everyone. Really appreciate your kind comments. Very glad you like the shot. I honestly didn''t think it''d do this well in a FS. It''s a wonerful pleasant surprise. None of the details in the shot where blurred (except selective noise removal in the sky), I did crop the sides and had two b/w conversions to choose from, one which had a lighter sky color, but playing with the channels I do like how the darker sky came out in this one but the feather detail was better in the color version. Also, updated the exif.', '2009-03-09 12:32:33.000000', '2009-03-09 12:40:42.000000', 0),
(5297659, 763997, 62357, '<td valign="top">So very sorry this didn''t score higher.  It was definitely one of my top scores in the whole FS.  Love it.</td>', 'So very sorry this didn''t score higher.  It was definitely one of my top scores in the whole FS.  Love it.', '2009-03-09 13:00:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297671, 767658, 32767, '<td valign="top"><b>They Came From The Planet Debbie</b> <br/> <br/>Very Ed Wood and a 4.8 to match. The 7''s represent a strong cult following.</td>', 'They Came From The Planet Debbie  Very Ed Wood and a 4.8 to match. The 7''s represent a strong cult following.', '2009-03-09 13:12:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297678, 762717, 61961, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Keith.  I took a look at your pbase gallery - some extraordinary shots there, too, including "Bad Hair Day" and "Snow Monkey 3."  And this ribbon-winning shot really stands out even more at a larger size.</td>', 'Congrats, Keith.  I took a look at your pbase gallery - some extraordinary shots there, too, including "Bad Hair Day" and "Snow Monkey 3."  And this ribbon-winning shot really stands out even more at a larger size.', '2009-03-09 13:20:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297694, 769247, 71167, '<td valign="top">WOW! Two Favorites!! Woot!<br/> <br/>Thank you all for your comments and votes! This was a last minute entry, I was traveling and had almost forgot to enter. I literally had 10 minutes to find and prep an image before the deadline. So, it was a quick photoshop b/w conversion, maybe a slight crop, nothing else by way of processing.<br/> <br/>If the eyes are the window to our soul then horses are often the key to our hearts. They are such noble, honest creatures.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-03-09 13:41:24.</i></td>', 'WOW! Two Favorites!! Woot! Thank you all for your comments and votes! This was a last minute entry, I was traveling and had almost forgot to enter. I literally had 10 minutes to find and prep an image before the deadline. So, it was a quick photoshop b/w conversion, maybe a slight crop, nothing else by way of processing. If the eyes are the window to our soul then horses are often the key to our hearts. They are such noble, honest creatures.', '2009-03-09 13:39:33.000000', '2009-03-09 13:41:24.000000', 0),
(5297721, 768547, 62357, '<td valign="top">I figured this was yours Rina.  I love it. Sorry it didn''t make it over 5.</td>', 'I figured this was yours Rina.  I love it. Sorry it didn''t make it over 5.', '2009-03-09 14:08:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297779, 762717, 64446, '<td valign="top">Supperb shot! I love the gallery too. Congratulations!!!</td>', 'Supperb shot! I love the gallery too. Congratulations!!!', '2009-03-09 14:53:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297816, 768443, 27475, '<td valign="top">Did any of the dogs lose its tongue?  My god they are out of control!!!<br/>Very very cool shot!!</td>', 'Did any of the dogs lose its tongue?  My god they are out of control!!!Very very cool shot!!', '2009-03-09 15:38:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297834, 766690, 17850, '<td valign="top">I could simply say congratulations for this image, but it wouldn''t be enough. It seems almost unbelievable to achieve such a detailed narrowband image using a DSLR instead of a dedicated astronomical monochrome CCD. <br/>I am curious on how you have placed the Ha, OIII and SII filters as there is only one filter wheel that can be attached to a DSLR (as far as I know) with only 2 positions. The other way is to take the specific set of frames replacing each filter, but then you may loose a significant amount of the original frame''s FOV, besause of the difference in orientation. <br/>Finally, I think that astronomical images like this belong to a different class and can not compare directly to any other kind of image here on DPC. So, keep up the good work John!</td>', 'I could simply say congratulations for this image, but it wouldn''t be enough. It seems almost unbelievable to achieve such a detailed narrowband image using a DSLR instead of a dedicated astronomical monochrome CCD. I am curious on how you have placed the Ha, OIII and SII filters as there is only one filter wheel that can be attached to a DSLR (as far as I know) with only 2 positions. The other way is to take the specific set of frames replacing each filter, but then you may loose a significant amount of the original frame''s FOV, besause of the difference in orientation. Finally, I think that astronomical images like this belong to a different class and can not compare directly to any other kind of image here on DPC. So, keep up the good work John!', '2009-03-09 16:01:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5297859, 767729, 30982, '<td valign="top">You must have quite the household full of animals!!  What fun!  This is a delightful shot.</td>', 'You must have quite the household full of animals!!  What fun!  This is a delightful shot.', '2009-03-09 16:22:48.000000', NULL, 0),
